  <!-- 7. Architecture ==================================================== -->
  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot">●</span> Architecture</p>
        <div class="col-r">
          <h2>A workspace, not a monolith.</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            Numra is organized in three layers. Each crate depends only
            on layers below it, so you can pull in just what you need
            without dragging in the whole numerical stack.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="arch">
        {archLayers.map((layer) => (
          <div class="arch-row">
            <div class="lhs">
              <span class="layer-num">{layer.num}</span>
              <span class="layer-name">{layer.name}</span>
              <span class="layer-tag">{layer.tag}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="rhs">
              {layer.crates.map((crate) => (
                <span class="crate"><b>{crate}</b></span>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 8. Engineering posture ============================================= -->
  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot">●</span> Engineering posture</p>
        <div class="col-r">
          <h2>Standards we hold ourselves to.</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            Three commitments across every release — provenance on
            every benchmark figure, regression tests against published
            invariants, and an explicit stability policy.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="eng-grid">
        <div class="eng-cell">
          <p class="h">01 · Provenance</p>
          <p class="t">Every figure carries a SHA.</p>
          <p class="b">
            Every benchmark plot in the book is annotated with the
            Numra commit, CPU model, rustc version, and a link to the
            reproduction script. Plots without that bar don't ship.
          </p>
          <a class="l" href="https://github.com/moussaoutlook/numra-rs/tree/main/numra-bench" rel="noopener">
            Bench harness →
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="eng-cell">
          <p class="h">02 · Tested</p>
          <p class="t">Invariants, not happy paths.</p>
          <p class="b">
            Convergence orders for ODE families, statistical bands for
            SDEs, golden-value LP/QP/MILP solutions, FFT round-trip,
            dense linear-solve smoke tests, and event localization.
          </p>
          <a class="l" href="/features">Feature matrix →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="eng-cell">
          <p class="h">03 · Stability</p>
          <p class="t">Pre-1.0 churn is documented.</p>
          <p class="b">
            Until 1.0, breaking changes carry rationale in the
            changelog. After 1.0, deprecation cycles run across at
            least one minor version before removal.
          </p>
          <a class="l" href="/stability">Stability policy →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 9. Where to start + cite =========================================== -->
